{title: 622 - Come, Come, Ye Saints}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]Come, come, ye saints, no toil nor labor fear;
[G]But [Em]with joy wend your [C/G]way.
[G]Though hard to you the journey [Am/C]may appear,
[Bm]Grace shall be as [Em/B]your day.
[G]We will have a living lord to guide,
[G]And we [Em]can trust Him to provide;
[G]Do this, and joy your hearts [Am/C]will swell:
[Bm]All is well! All [Em/B]is well!

Verse 2:
[G]We'll find the rest which God for us prepared,
[G]When [Em]at last He will [C/G]call;
[G]Where none will come to hurt or [Am/C]make afraid,
[Bm]He will reign over [Em/B]all.
[G]We will make the air with music ring,
[G]Shout praise [Em]to God our Lord and [C/G]King:
[G]O how we'll make the chorus [Am/C]swell:
[Bm]All is well! All [Em/B]is well!
